specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:143:- A frame that fails validation and is not a `user_message`, such as a malformed `ping`, gets its `INVALID_MESSAGE` at once, even while a run is pending, but a `user_message` that fails validation is answered in turn, its `INVALID_MESSAGE` and `stream_end` after the run in progress, since an `error` frame names no message and would otherwise read as the running answer's ([validated by: answers an invalid ping at once but an invalid user_message in turn, after the run in progress](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L708), [validated by: answers a malformed user_message in turn with INVALID_MESSAGE then stream_end when a store is threaded](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L90)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:144:- The reconnect flush (§ 11.3), which sends queued messages in one burst, is therefore safe: they are answered one after another, in the order the user typed them ([validated by: queues three messages sent in one tick before the handler returns, and answers them in that order](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L724)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:145:- A queued message whose socket has closed by the time its turn comes is dropped, neither recorded nor answered, since nobody is left to read the answer and a session whose last socket closed has no credentials left ([validated by: drops a queued message whose socket closed before its turn, without asking the model or recording it](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L741)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:344:- A message the server cannot parse into a known type is answered with `INVALID_MESSAGE`, and no message stream is started for it ([validated by: rejects an unparseable message and never starts a stream](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L71)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:350:Response to a client `ping`. The server MUST echo the client's timestamp without modification ([validated by: answers a ping with the timestamp it was given](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L81)).
specs/hal-engine-websocket-protocol/spec.md:529:- A reply with no tool calls and no thinking produces, in order, the user entry, the assistant entry opened empty, one `entry_delta` per text chunk, its `entry_commit`, and `stream_end` ([validated by: sends the user entry, then the assistant entry, its delta, its commit and stream_end](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L91)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-executor-throw/spec.md:36:- **NIS-2 Article 21, operational resilience.** Over the WebSocket, a turn whose tool name was invented streams its answer and ends with `stream_end`, never an `error` frame ([validated by: completes a turn whose tool name the model invented: its answer streams, then stream_end, with no error frame](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L819)).
specs/hal-engine-tool-executor-throw/spec.md:37:- So does a turn whose tool executor threw: one broken tool degrades one answer instead of ending the conversation ([validated by: completes a turn whose tool executor threw: its answer streams, then stream_end, with no error frame](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L825)).
specs/hal-engine-single-terminal-frame/spec.md:18:- A valid `ping` produces `pong` and no `stream_end` ([validated by: answers a ping with the timestamp it was given](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L81)).
specs/hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md:13:- The message handler hands that signal on to the run, as `processMessageStream`'s `signal` ([validated by: hands the run its connection signal](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L789)).
specs/hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md:19:- No `error` and no `stream_end` follow the close, since nobody is left to read a terminal frame. The answer cut off is committed as it stood and flagged `truncated: true`, so it is re-sent and committed, the two frames any cut-off answer gets, here written to a closed socket ([validated by: abandons the turn mid-stream with no error and no stream_end, committing the cut-off answer as it stood](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L758)).
specs/hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md:22:- A message queued behind the turn, or handed over after the close, is dropped: nothing is recorded, the orchestrator is never asked and nothing is sent ([validated by: drops a turn whose connection signal is already aborted: records nothing, asks nothing, sends nothing](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L776)).
specs/hal-engine-abandon-on-close/spec.md:23:- A `ping` is answered whatever the signal ([validated by: answers a ping whose connection signal is aborted](../../src/transport/ws/messageHandler.test.ts#L809)).
